Third-party projects this work builds upon, compares against, or was informed by
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. gvergine/qnx-fs-9p — Apache-2.0
   https://github.com/gvergine/qnx-fs-9p
   A complete 9P2000.L client for QNX guests, ARM64 only (virtio-mmio).
   Relationship to Passerelle: prior art, cited in the README and in
   docs/state-of-the-art.md; benchmarked by host/bench; the PCI transport and
   x86_64 target that Passerelle adds are offered back to this project as
   patches under upstream/qnx-fs-9p/. No source file of this project is copied
   into Passerelle. Numeric facts that cannot be copyrighted (Linux errno
   numbers, 9P2000.L message numbers and field orders, virtio capability
   layouts) were cross-checked against its documentation and sources.

2. eclipse-score/qnx_unit_tests, directory src/common/virtio9p — Apache-2.0
   https://github.com/eclipse-score/qnx_unit_tests
   A 9P client for x86_64 and ARM64 reduced to what unit tests need. It is the
   public reference for programming MSI-X on QNX without a root PCI server
   configuration; that method is described (not copied) in
   docs/design/transport.md and exercised by the E1 feasibility test.

3. kodebooth/qnx-virtio — MIT
   https://github.com/kodebooth/qnx-virtio
   A virtio transport library for QNX 8 (core, queues, PCI, MMIO) with a sample
   GPIO driver. Evaluated for reuse as decision D3 of the specification; the
   evaluation and its outcome are recorded in docs/decisions.md. Passerelle
   ships its own transport because every layer must also build and run its tests
   on the PC (requirement P9-10), which requires a bus-access abstraction that
   this project does not provide.

4. The FUSE kernel ABI — (GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note) OR BSD-2-Clause
   /usr/include/linux/fuse.h, Copyright (C) 2001-2008 Miklos Szeredi
   protofuse/fusep_abi.h re-states the wire layout of the FUSE protocol in our
   own words and our own field names. No line of the Linux header is copied;
   the header is only used as the authoritative description of the layout.

5. The 9P2000.L protocol description — diod project
   https://github.com/chaos/diod/blob/master/protocol.md
   Used as the normative description of message layouts for 9P2000.L.

6. QEMU 9p/virtio-fs documentation
   https://wiki.qemu.org/Documentation/9psetup
   https://wiki.qemu.org/Documentation/9p
   https://virtio-fs.gitlab.io/howto-qemu.html
   Used for host-side setup, security models and message-size guidance.

